From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iam <iam@iashur.internal>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 05:29:51 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] input: add global recenter via held menu button

No dashboard/vrmonitor exists in this reimplementation, so there was no
way to recenter a game that doesn't expose its own in-game recenter
option -- SLAM origin drift just stayed baked in for the whole session.
Real SteamVR provides this globally via its dashboard, intercepting the
button before the game ever sees it.

Adds Input::check_system_recenter_hold, called once per frame from
frame_start_update for any game using the legacy input path: if the
real physical menu button is held 3s (XRIZER_RECENTER_HOLD_SECS to
override), calls the existing (and already working)
OpenXrData::reset_tracking_space(Standing).

Two real bugs found and fixed via live testing on WMR hardware before
this worked correctly:

- First version reused the existing app_menu action directly. On the
  oculus/touch_controller profile (what WMR controllers present as),
  app_menu is bound to the Y/B face buttons, not the real physical menu
  button -- the hold was never detected. Fixed by adding a dedicated
  system_recenter action, bound only to the real menu button where one
  exists per profile, and deliberately never read by
  get_legacy_controller_state, so it stays fully invisible to games.
  (An even earlier attempt bound the real menu button directly into
  app_menu instead of a separate action -- that broke in-game input
  outright: every recenter hold also delivered a real ApplicationMenu
  press to the game, which several titles interpret as "toggle pause".)

- reset_tracking_space(Standing) sets the new origin's position
  directly from the current head pose, including height -- this
  clobbered any height/floor calibration a game had already done at
  startup, leaving the player noticeably too low afterward. Standing
  recenter should only fix horizontal position and facing direction,
  the same way real SteamVR's room-scale recenter leaves floor height
  alone (Seated is unaffected -- eye height is part of what seated
  calibration is expected to set). reset_tracking_space now takes a
  preserve_height flag, zeroing the Y offset for Standing only.

Confirmed live: VRSailing by BeTomorrow (was ~4m from its expected
play-space center) recenters correctly with real height preserved,
and normal gameplay input (trigger, movement, etc.) is unaffected by
holding the recenter button.

Signed-off-by: brunduk <nikolai.viktorovich@gmail.com>
